# Switch the answering node into one of the modes it reported via ListControllers.
#
# This is a CONTROL-LAW switch only. It must never arm/disarm a vehicle or change the
# PX4 flight mode -- those stay with the RC/ELRS transmitter on real hardware.
#
# Requesting the already-active mode succeeds and is a no-op, so a caller retrying
# after a lost response cannot bounce the controller.

# Must match a ControllerInfo.name from ListControllers. Unknown names are rejected
# rather than silently mapped to a default.
string name
---
bool success
string message

# The mode actually active after handling the request. On failure this is the mode
# still running, so a caller always learns the true state -- do not assume a sent
# request took effect; confirm from this field or the controller_type topic.
string active
